1
00:00:14,500 --> 00:00:16,935
[vi] Good morning, everyone.

2
00:00:17,835 --> 00:00:20,090
[vi] Did you sleep well?

3
00:00:21,240 --> 00:00:23,945
[vi] Barely. The storm kept me up.

4
00:00:25,345 --> 00:00:28,005
[vi] We should leave before noon.

5
00:00:28,905 --> 00:00:31,700
[vi] The road south is still closed.

6
00:00:32,850 --> 00:00:35,285
[vi] Then we take the river.

7
00:00:36,685 --> 00:00:39,795
[vi] Is that even possible in this weather?

8
00:00:40,695 --> 00:00:42,950
[vi] It is the only way.

9
00:00:44,100 --> 00:00:46,985
[vi] I counted four boats at the dock.

10
00:00:48,385 --> 00:00:50,640
[vi] Three of them leak.

11
00:00:51,540 --> 00:00:53,750
[vi] Of course they do.

12
00:00:54,900 --> 00:00:57,740
[vi] Take the one with the blue sail.

13
00:00:59,140 --> 00:01:01,530
[vi] You are enjoying this.

14
00:01:02,430 --> 00:01:04,235
[vi] A little.

15
00:01:05,385 --> 00:01:07,865
[vi] What about the supplies?

16
00:01:09,265 --> 00:01:11,340
[vi] Already loaded.

17
00:01:12,240 --> 00:01:14,270
[vi] And the radio?

18
00:01:15,420 --> 00:01:18,215
[vi] Dead battery. I left it behind.

19
00:01:19,615 --> 00:01:21,690
[vi] We will manage.

20
00:01:22,590 --> 00:01:25,430
[vi] That is what you said last time.

21
00:01:26,580 --> 00:01:28,700
[vi] And we survived.

22
00:01:30,100 --> 00:01:31,860
[vi] By luck.

23
00:01:32,760 --> 00:01:34,700
[vi] Luck counts.

24
00:01:35,850 --> 00:01:38,015
[vi] Look at that sky.

25
00:01:39,415 --> 00:01:41,445
[vi] It is turning.

26
00:01:42,345 --> 00:01:44,735
[vi] We have maybe an hour.

27
00:01:45,885 --> 00:01:48,860
[vi] Then stop talking and start rowing.

28
00:01:50,260 --> 00:01:52,110
[vi] After you.

29
00:01:53,010 --> 00:01:55,400
[vi] Careful with the rope.

30
00:01:56,550 --> 00:01:59,030
[vi] I have done this before.

31
00:02:00,430 --> 00:02:03,045
[vi] Not in a current like this.

32
00:02:03,945 --> 00:02:06,605
[vi] Watch the rocks on the left.

33
00:02:07,755 --> 00:02:09,650
[vi] I see them.

34
00:02:11,050 --> 00:02:13,260
[vi] Hard to starboard!

35
00:02:14,160 --> 00:02:15,740
[vi] Now!

36
00:02:16,890 --> 00:02:18,965
[vi] That was close.

37
00:02:20,365 --> 00:02:22,215
[vi] Too close.

38
00:02:23,115 --> 00:02:25,280
[vi] The hull is fine.

39
00:02:26,430 --> 00:02:28,775
[vi] The hull is not fine.

40
00:02:30,175 --> 00:02:32,610
[vi] We are taking on water.

41
00:02:33,510 --> 00:02:35,765
[vi] Bail. I will steer.

42
00:02:36,915 --> 00:02:38,900
[vi] For how long?

43
00:02:40,300 --> 00:02:42,780
[vi] Until we reach the bend.

44
00:02:43,680 --> 00:02:46,475
[vi] There is a cabin past the bend.

45
00:02:47,625 --> 00:02:49,970
[vi] Empty since the fire.

46
00:02:51,370 --> 00:02:53,220
[vi] Not empty.

47
00:02:54,120 --> 00:02:56,375
[vi] You are impossible.

48
00:02:57,525 --> 00:02:59,555
[vi] I am prepared.
